caption: Quick Start — Five Rules to Remember
technology-rule: five-rules-to-remember

| Common Mistake | Correct Rule |
| --- | --- |
| All cybernetics receive a discount | No. Apply only limitations that create real restrictions in play. |
| A visible implant is automatically Class III | No. Visible but species-anatomical modifications are Class II. |
| A strong arm grants full-body strength | No. Use Arm ST until the spine, hips, legs, power, and control systems support broader ST. |
| Money can buy any advantage | Money buys access and hardware; character points buy reliable personal capability. |
| Onboard power is automatically a Gadget | No. Use Accessibility, Costs FP or ER, Takes Recharge, Limited Use, or Dependency as appropriate. Gadget applies only when the component is externally breakable or separately damageable, removable, or destructible. |
